>115</volume>:<fpage>4649</fpage>&#x02013;4660.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12415009</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal">Femino, A.M., F.S. Fay, K. Fogarty, and R.H. Singer. <year>1998</year>. Visualization of single RNA transcripts in situ. <source>Science.</source> <volume>280</volume>:<fpage>585</fpage>&#x02013;590.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9554849</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Femino, A.M., K. Fogarty, L.M. Lifshitz, W. Carrington, and R.H. Singer. <year>2003</year>. Visualization of single molecules of mRNA in situ. <source>Methods Enzymol.</source> <volume>361</volume>:<fpage>245</fpage>&#x02013;304.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12624916</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Fusco, D., N. Accornero, B. Lavoie, S.M. Shenoy, J.M. Blanchard, R.H. Singer, and E. Bertrand. <year>2003</year>. Single mRNA molecules demonstrate probabilistic movement in living mammalian cells. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>161</fpage>&#x02013;167.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12546792</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Gaietta, G., T.J. Deerinck, S.R. Adams, J. Bouwer, O. Tour, D.W. Laird, G.E. Sosinsky, R.Y. Tsien, and M.H. Ellisman. <year>2002</year>. Multicolor and electron microscopic imaging of connexin trafficking. <source>Science.</source> <volume>296</volume>:<fpage>503</fpage>&#x02013;507.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11964472</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Geisbrecht, E.R., and D.J. Montell. <year>2002</year>. Myosin VI is required for E-cadherin-mediated border cell migration. <source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>4</volume>:<fpage>616</fpage>&#x02013;620.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12134162</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Godchaux, W., III, S.D. Adamson, and E. Herbert. <year>1967</year>. Effects of cycloheximide on polyribosome function in reticulocytes. <source>J. Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>27</volume>:<fpage>57</fpage>&#x02013;72.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6033612</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Gupton, S.L., K.L. Anderson, T.P. Kole, R.S. Fischer, A. Ponti, S.E. Hitchcock-DeGregori, G. Danuser, V.M. Fowler, D. Wirtz, D. Hanein, and C.M. Waterman-Storer. <year>2005</year>. Cell migration without a lamellipodium: translation of actin dynamics into cell movement mediated by tropomyosin. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>168</volume>:<fpage>619</fpage>&#x02013;631.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15716379</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Hill, M.A., and P. Gunning. <year>1993</year>. &#x003b2; and &#x003b3; actin mRNAs are differentially located within myoblasts. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>122</volume>:<fpage>825</fpage>&#x02013;832.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8349732</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Hofer, D., W. Ness, and D. Drenckhahn. <year>1997</year>. Sorting of actin isoforms in chicken auditory hair cells. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>110</volume>:<fpage>765</fpage>&#x02013;770.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9099950</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Huttelmaier, S., D. Zenklusen, M. Lederer, J. Dictenberg, M. Lorenz, X. Meng, G.J. Bassell, J. Condeelis, and R.H. Singer. <year>2005</year>. Spatial regulation of beta-actin translation by Src-dependent phosphorylation of ZBP1. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>438</volume>:<fpage>512</fpage>&#x02013;515.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16306994</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Job, C., and J. Eberwine. <year>2001</year>. Localization and translation of mRNA in dendrites and axons. <source>Nat. Rev. Neurosci.</source> <volume>2</volume>:<fpage>889</fpage>&#x02013;898.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11733796</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Joklik, W.K., and Y. Becker. <year>1965</year>. Studies on the genesis of polyribosomes. I. Origin and significance of the subribosomal particles. <source>J. Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>496</fpage>&#x02013;510.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5867032</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Ju, W., W. Morishita, J. Tsui, G. Gaietta, T.J. Deerinck, S.R. Adams, C.C. Garner, R.Y. Tsien, M.H. Ellisman, and R.C. Malenka. <year>2004</year>. Activity-dependent regulation of dendritic synthesis and trafficking of AMPA receptors. <source>Nat. Neurosci.</source> <volume>7</volume>:<fpage>244</fpage>&#x02013;253.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14770185</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Kislauskis, E.H., Z. Li, R.H. Singer, and K.L. Taneja. <year>1993</year>. Isoform-specific 3&#x02032;-untranslated sequences sort &#x003b1;-cardiac and &#x003b2;-cytoplasmic actin messenger RNAs to different cytoplasmic compartments. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>123</volume>:<fpage>165</fpage>&#x02013;172.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8408195</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Kislauskis, E.H., X. Zhu, and R.H. Singer. <year>1994</year>. Sequences responsible for intracellular localization of &#x003b2;-actin messenger RNA also affect cell phenotype. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>127</volume>:<fpage>441</fpage>&#x02013;451.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7929587</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Kislauskis, E.H., X. Zhu, and R.H. Singer. <year>1997</year>. &#x003b2;-Actin messenger RNA localization and protein synthesis augment cell motility. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>136</volume>:<fpage>1263</fpage>&#x02013;1270.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9087442</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Latham, V.M., E.H. Yu, A.N. Tullio, R.S. Adelstein, and R.H. Singer. <year>2001</year>. A Rho-dependent signaling pathway operating through myosin localizes beta-actin mRNA in fibroblasts. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>11</volume>:<fpage>1010</fpage>&#x02013;1016.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11470405</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Lawrence, J.B., and R.H. Singer. <year>1986</year>. Intracellular localization of messenger RNAs for cytoskeletal proteins. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>45</volume>:<fpage>407</fpage>&#x02013;415.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3698103</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Lenk, R., L. Ransom, Y. Kaufmann, and S. Penman. <year>1977</year>. A cytoskeletal structure with associated polyribosomes obtained from HeLa cells. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>10</volume>:<fpage>67</fpage>&#x02013;78.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">837445</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Lodish, H.F. <year>1971</year>. Alpha and beta globin messenger ribonucleic acid. Different amounts and rates of initiation of translation. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>246</volume>:<fpage>7131</fpage>&#x02013;7138.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5167019</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Lodish, H.F., and A. Jacobson. <year>1972</year>. Translational control of protein synthesis in eukaryotic cells: is there tissue or species specificity of the translational apparatus? <source>Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>27</volume>:<fpage>283</fpage>&#x02013;285.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5019940</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Macchi, P., I. Hemraj, B. Goetze, B. Grunewald, M. Mallardo, and M.A. Kiebler. <year>2003</year>. A GFP-based system to uncouple mRNA transport from translation in a single living neuron. <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>14</volume>:<fpage>1570</fpage>&#x02013;1582.<pub-id pub-i